            <ArticleTitle>Intraspinal schwannoma presenting solely with rectal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>417-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A cauda equina schwannoma presented solely with rectal pain. The tumor was found to have infarcted and hemorrhaged. A discussion of rectal pain is included, and it is speculated that some forms of rectal pain, especially those classified as proctalgia fugax or rectal neuralgia, may be due to cauda equina tumors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
